# SEALED G1 heldout split (AD-13).
#
# This directory holds the sealed G1 evaluation set. It is NEVER consumed by any routine CI
# job in ci.yml or canary.yml. The benchmark runner refuses to touch it without an explicit
# gate-exit flag, and only a manually-dispatched gate-exit workflow (added at Gate G1 exit,
# Story 2.4) may pass that flag. Do NOT add a CI glob that sweeps this path.
#
# The sealing machinery lands in Story 2.4. The ONLY content that may land here is the sealed
# pair — `heldout.tar.enc` (key-bound, SHA-verified archive) + `SEAL.json` (the manifest) — plus
# this `.gitkeep`. A raw live case file (`case.yaml`, `fixture.FCStd`, an eval question) must NEVER
# land here unsealed; `gate run G1 --exit` is the only path that unseals, always into a temp dir it
# deletes afterward.
#
# No live held-out cases exist yet — the split is authored by a human ceremony (`gate seal G1`
# after cases are staged), so the committed seal may be a `case_count: 0` placeholder.
